      "importance": "high",
      "content": {
        "shape": "cylinder",
        "label": "Redis",
        "kind": "store",
        "sublabel": "Cached price lists, all rebuildable"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n-broker",
      "type": "shape",
      "parent": "g-persistence",
      "importance": "high",
      "content": {
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "label": "Message broker",
        "kind": "messagebus",
        "sublabel": "StockReserved events; dead-letter queue"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n-supplier",
      "type": "shape",
      "parent": "g-persistence",
      "importance": "high",
      "content": {
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "label": "Supplier API",
        "kind": "external",
        "sublabel": "External: run by the suppliers"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g-gaps",
      "type": "group",
      "content": {
        "label": "Known gaps",
        "arrangement": "grid",
        "takeaway": "Unverified or missing today"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n-gaps",
      "type": "text",
      "parent": "g-gaps",
      "importance": "medium",
      "title": "Known gaps",
      "content": {
        "markdown": "- Orchestrator and adapter can change the same stock at once; the ledger relies on a database row lock; whether the row lock holds under peak load has not been measured.\n- No alert when `inventory.dlq` fills up: dead-lettered deliveries are found only in the admin UI.\n- The admin UI has no automated tests yet."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g-integration",
      "type": "group",
      "content": {
        "label": "Supplier integration",
        "arrangement": "stack",
        "takeaway": "The only module that knows the supplier format",
        "diagram": "architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n-adapter",
      "type": "shape",
      "parent": "g-integration",
      "importance": "high",
      "content": {
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "label": "Supplier feed adapter",
        "kind": "backend",
        "sublabel": "src/suppliers/feedAdapter.ts",
        "details": [
          "Every 10 minutes: deliveries become restocks",
          "Unparseable deliveries are logged and skipped; they aren't retried"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g-obs",
      "type": "group",
      "content": {
        "label": "Observability & error handling",
        "arrangement": "stack",
        "takeaway": "One structured log; retries only for supplier calls",
        "diagram": "architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n-logger",
      "type": "shape",
      "parent": "g-obs",
      "importance": "high",
      "content": {
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "label": "Structured logger",
        "kind": "backend",
        "sublabel": "src/platform/log.ts",
        "details": [
          "One JSON line per event, always with the correlation ID"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n-retry",
      "type": "shape",
      "parent": "g-obs",
      "importance": "high",
      "content": {
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "label": "Retry helper",
        "kind": "backend",
        "sublabel": "src/platform/retry.ts",
        "details": [
          "Wraps supplier calls"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n-policy",
      "type": "text",
      "parent": "g-obs",
      "importance": "low",
      "title": "Retry policy",
      "content": {
        "markdown": "- At most **5 attempts** per delivery\n- Exponential backoff: starts at **2 seconds**, doubles after each failure, capped at **60 seconds**\n- After the 5th failure: published to `inventory.dlq`, reviewed by staff in the admin UI\n\nApplies only to supplier calls. Reservations are never retried: a failed reservation goes back to the caller as an error."
      }
    }
  ],
